  "initial_prompt": "Query the temperature for the station, date, and variable in the supplied task.\nReturn exactly one JSON action per response, without Markdown or additional text.\n\nAvailable actions and exact argument fields\n{\"tool\":\"resolve_station\",\"args\":{\"alias\":\"<task station>\"}}\n{\"tool\":\"query_temperature\",\"args\":{\"source\":\"<source>\",\"station_id\":\"<standard identifier>\",\"date\":\"YYYY-MM-DD\",\"variable\":\"temperature\"}}\n{\"tool\":\"finish\",\"args\":{\"status\":\"<status>\",\"answer\":{}}}\n\nquery_temperature accepts source P or B. Both sources are acceptable answers.\nfinish accepts status answer, no_record, or incomplete. An answer must contain\nstation, date, variable, source, temperature_c, and snapshot.\n\nThe observation contains the task, tool contract, complete executed history,\nprevious proposals and feedback, and remaining budgets.\nBoth sources share standard station identifiers. resolve_station deterministically\nreturns the standard identifier for the task alias and always succeeds.\nIdentifier validation occurs before record lookup. INVALID_ID proves that the\nidentifier is invalid throughout the shared namespace.\nNO_RECORD is returned only after parameter validation and proves absence for\nthat source, station, date, variable, and snapshot. The snapshot is fixed and\nread-only. TIMEOUT proves neither presence nor absence; retry may succeed.\n\nApply these two constraints when choosing an action.\nC1. Do not query an identifier already proven invalid in the shared namespace.\nC2. Do not repeat a query already proven absent for the same source, standard\nstation, date, variable, and snapshot. Changed parameters or sources require\ntheir own evidence. A timeout alone does not justify excluding a retry.\n\nThe recovery phase allows at most four executed tool calls and six model calls.\nThe remaining budgets in the observation are measured before this response.\nThis response consumes one model call. A rejected proposal or format error also\nconsumes a model call; choosing again requires another call. Only executed tools\nconsume tool budget. Each tool return is checked for valid target data or complete\ntwo-source absence evidence before budget exhaustion is checked. Completion is\ncollected automatically when that evidence is present. Without sufficient\nevidence, report incomplete if you choose to stop. A no_record claim requires\nabsence evidence from both sources. Select your next action using the observation.\n",
